{"h":3395,"w":2400,"lines":[{"h":0.008720930389296444,"y":0.046511627815394085,"c":0.5,"t":"1718867188","x":0.7716049391467531,"w":0.069958845774332645},{"c":1,"y":0.097383720806266338,"t":"READING PASSAGE 3","x":0.10082304673545198,"w":0.21193415323893225,"h":0.013081395583944722},{"c":1,"t":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 27-40, which are based on Reading","x":0.10288066772756499,"w":0.77160491943359366,"y":0.12926972885502652,"h":0.017667844522968212},{"w":0.15843621571858726,"t":"Passage 3 below.","y":0.14680232543732186,"c":1,"x":0.10288065742610494,"h":0.014563987898180697},{"t":"Timur Gareyev - blindfold chess champion","x":0.19341563995261349,"y":0.18313953524528293,"w":0.59670781453450528,"c":1,"h":0.021807461661079275},{"y":0.22084805635159399,"t":"Next month, a chess player named Timur Gareyev will take on nearly 50 opponents","w":0.7366255187988282,"h":0.016195524146054185,"x":0.14403291949233638,"c":1},{"c":1,"w":0.71810699462890626,"t":"at once. But that is not the hard part. While his challengers will play the games as","x":0.14403292232934745,"y":0.23837209288981276,"h":0.014572547939556646},{"w":0.69547322591145833,"h":0.01598837238037687,"x":0.14403293427481667,"t":"normal, Gareyev himself will be blindfolded. Even by world record standards, it","c":1,"y":0.25436046497001508},{"x":0.14403293050013027,"w":0.72016459147135437,"y":0.27179034161532301,"t":"sets a high bar for human performance. The 28-year-old already stands out in the","h":0.014546867815428799,"c":1},{"h":0.01472320376914027,"y":0.28769140139769722,"w":0.72839508056640623,"t":"rarefied world of blindfold chess. He has a fondness for bright clothes and unusual","c":1,"x":0.14403291225067658},{"y":0.3028778530979096,"x":0.14397882676065402,"w":0.73468750000000005,"c":1,"t":"hairstyles, and he gets his kicks from the adventure sport of BASE jumping. He has","h":0.018577433025598222},{"h":0.01598837238037687,"c":1,"w":0.72222223917643225,"y":0.32122093008639863,"x":0.14403291323614553,"t":"already proved himself a strong chess player, too. In a 10-hour chess marathon in"},{"t":"2013, Gareyev played 33 games in his head simultaneously. He won 29 and lost","x":0.14396745213687684,"c":1,"y":0.33602128131849396,"w":0.71208562215169269,"h":0.018794076602787535},{"y":0.35453474699330112,"t":"none. The skill has become his brand: he calls himself the Blindfold King.","x":0.14403291637458948,"h":0.014723203769140047,"c":1,"w":0.64609054565429691},{"t":"But Gareyev's prowess has drawn interest from beyond the chess-playing","x":0.14403291531428428,"w":0.65226338704427078,"c":1,"y":0.38662790682507331,"h":0.01598837238037687},{"x":0.14403291417998806,"y":0.40400471133129501,"t":"community. In the hope of understanding how he and others like him can perform","w":0.71604939778645826,"c":1,"h":0.01472320376914027},{"h":0.014570836043610536,"c":1,"x":0.14609054305001259,"w":0.66872426350911462,"t":"such mental feats, researchers at the University of California in Los Angeles","y":0.42005813940122771},{"y":0.43749999985376098,"c":1,"t":"(UCLA) called him in for tests. They now have their first results. 'The ability to play","x":0.14197531637540597,"w":0.72633743286132812,"h":0.01598837238037687},{"h":0.016002068109590928,"y":0.45347467621727722,"w":0.70370371500651041,"t":"a game of chess with your eyes closed is not a far reach for most accomplished","x":0.1440329160630292,"c":1},{"w":0.73456792195638032,"y":0.46937573598684346,"c":1,"h":0.017667844522968212,"x":0.14609052449598106,"t":"players,' said Jesse Rissman, who runs a memory lab at UCLA. 'But the thing that's"},{"x":0.14602353256388634,"w":0.73475107828776043,"c":1,"h":0.017895984986645574,"t":"so remarkable about Timur and a few other individuals is the number of games they","y":0.48402140263648108},{"w":0.49416549682617178,"c":1,"x":0.14388385749373361,"y":0.50138645012695882,"t":"can keep active at once. To me it is simply astonishing.'","h":0.020644147488759201},{"x":0.14609052545694623,"y":0.53621908104795046,"w":0.72839508056640623,"c":1,"h":0.014723203769140158,"t":"Gareyev learned to play chess in his native Uzbekistan when he was six years old."},{"h":0.016008916255020766,"t":"Tutored by his grandfather, he entered his first tournament aged eight and soon","y":0.55377906962123535,"x":0.14403293331710443,"w":0.70164606730143231,"c":1},{"w":0.72222223917643225,"x":0.14403291327335532,"t":"became obsessed with competitions. At 16, he was crowned Asia's youngest ever","y":0.56976744171152904,"h":0.015988372380376759,"c":1},{"t":"chess grandmaster. He moved to the US soon after, and as a student helped his","y":0.58443874504730708,"w":0.71003682454427075,"x":0.14394879821822865,"h":0.019705027657768381,"c":1},{"y":0.59908592490330803,"h":0.022687485136609564,"t":"university win its first national chess championship. In 2013, Gareyev was ranked","x":0.14391678334447419,"c":1,"w":0.71834009806315102},{"t":"the third best chess player in the US.","h":0.01598837238037687,"c":1,"x":0.14403292653635957,"y":0.6191860463484532,"w":0.33127571105957032},{"y":0.65253239096767746,"c":1,"h":0.016195524146054185,"x":0.10082304735804209,"t":"D To the uninitiated, blindfold chess seems to call for superhuman skill. But displays","w":0.7633744812011718},{"y":0.66860465101665412,"w":0.69135803222656256,"h":0.016024324441826665,"x":0.14403291794053322,"t":"of the feat go back centuries. The first recorded game in Europe was played in","c":1},{"h":0.017441860778592888,"y":0.68604651146856543,"w":0.73045267740885422,"t":"13th-century Florence. In 1947, the Argentinian grandmaster Miguel Najdorf played","c":1,"x":0.14609053361453361},{"h":0.016020899526643317,"y":0.70200235570945757,"t":"45 simultaneous games in his mind, winning 39 in the 24-hour session.","w":0.62962961832682285,"c":1,"x":0.1440329259394692},{"w":0.7162303161621093,"x":0.14394972756425167,"y":0.73399675953780441,"c":1,"h":0.018385699556348389,"t":"Accomplished players can develop the skill of playing blind even without realising"},{"y":0.75290697662450179,"h":0.013081395583944722,"c":1,"w":0.68312759399414058,"t":"it. The nature of the game is to run through possible moves in the mind to see","x":0.14609052387999563},{"t":"how they play out. From this, regular players develop a memory for the patterns","c":1,"x":0.14403291603950369,"w":0.70370371500651041,"h":0.016038020171040834,"y":0.76884570090013071},{"c":1,"x":0.14397666203966764,"w":0.68736857096354165,"h":0.018915295460479653,"t":"the pieces make, the defences and attacks. 'You recreate it in your mind,' said","y":0.78331499172338537},{"c":1,"x":0.14600983657388289,"h":0.019612216837133767,"y":0.79894066365877991,"t":"Gareyev. 'A lot of players are capable of doing what I'm doing.' The real mental","w":0.69563313802083337},{"x":0.14609054458964096,"t":"challenge comes from playing multiple games at once in the head. Not only must","w":0.71399175008138005,"y":0.81831395335500401,"h":0.01453488398216074,"c":1},{"x":0.14403293238299189,"y":0.83568904593406512,"w":0.70781890869140629,"c":1,"h":0.016195524146054185,"t":"the positions of each piece on every board be memorised, they must be recalled"},{"h":0.013081395583944722,"c":1,"y":0.86773255796252025,"x":0.8580246914705375,"t":"89","w":0.024691357612609877},{"w":0.30619837443033859,"t":"IELTSXpress.com","c":1,"x":0.66984496081179823,"y":0.95314993691982619,"h":0.035152653221247165}]}